   "body": "Thanks, this looks careful. Skipping whole runs only when the ray misses their grown box is sound, and the old include is a good reference to check it against. CI is green. Two things before I merge:\n\n- `vendor/` is excluded from the workspace, and truck-meshalgo's lib tests don't build on their own (they read `../resources/shape/bottle.json`), so `include_same_as_before` never runs, either here or in CI. Could you move the comparison into a test that runs? For example, a `#[cfg(test)]` hook exercised from a kernel test, like the other vendored fixes do.\n- Please fill in the description: what you measured, and on which face, before and after. Tessellation is also being reworked for display quality right now (#1287, which landed as #1319), so I'd like numbers on current main.",
